{"term":"attend","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a1f11b5097d8e78af5","definition":"Senses relating to caring for or waiting on someone, or accompanying or being present.","example":"The fift [beadsman] had charge ſick perſons to attend, / And comfort thoſe, in point of death vvhich lay; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["attendable","attended","attendee","attender","attending","attend to","coattend","disattend","misattend","overattend","preattend","reattend","reattendance","reattender","stretch-attend posture","tend","underattend"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attend#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1aebb99008c1c3e0be","definition":"Senses relating to directing one's attention.","example":"Pyrocles minde was all thius while so fixed upon another devotion, that he no more attentively marked his friends discourse, then […] the diligent pilot in a dangerous tempest doth attend the unskilful words of a passinger: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["behear"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["attendable","attended","attendee","attender","attending","attend to","coattend","disattend","misattend","overattend","preattend","reattend","reattendance","reattender","stretch-attend posture","tend","underattend"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attend#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:df43978054e14f2476","definition":"Senses relating to waiting for something.","example":"Ægyptian ingenuity vvas more unſatisfied, contriving their bodies in ſvveet conſiſtences, to attend the return of their ſouls. But all vvas vanity, feeding the vvinde, and folly.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abide","attend","await","bide","expect","h